Body:
Here is the fix. The root cause is in `packages/opencode/src/mcp/catalog.ts` — the `convertTool` function passes `inputSchema` directly to the `ai` package's `jsonSchema()`, which uses AJV internally. AJV warns about non-standard format specifiers like `google-duration` and `uint64`.

The fix: strip unknown format fields from the schema before `jsonSchema()` sees them.

In `packages/opencode/src/mcp/catalog.ts`, add a helper and use it in `convertTool`:

```typescript
const KNOWN_FORMATS = new Set([
  'date-time', 'date', 'time', 'duration',
  'email', 'idn-email',
  'hostname', 'idn-hostname', 'ipv4', 'ipv6',
  'uri', 'uri-reference', 'uri-template', 'iri', 'iri-reference',
  'json-pointer', 'relative-json-pointer',
  'regex', 'uuid',
])

function stripUnknownFormats(schema: JSONSchema7): JSONSchema7 {
  if (typeof schema !== 'object' || schema === null) return schema
  const result: Record<string, unknown> = {}
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(schema)) {
    if (key === 'format' && typeof value === 'string' && !KNOWN_FORMATS.has(value)) {
      continue
    }
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      result[key] = value.map((v) => stripUnknownFormats(v as JSONSchema7))
    } else if (typeof value === 'object' && value !== null) {
      result[key] = stripUnknownFormats(value as JSONSchema7)
    } else {
      result[key] = value
    }
  }
  return result as JSONSchema7
}
```

Then modify `convertTool` to apply `stripUnknownFormats` to the input schema before passing to `jsonSchema()`.

This is the same approach as PR #12815 adapted to the current codebase. The `ai` SDK's `jsonSchema()` validates the schema with AJV — non-standard formats like `google-duration` and `uint64` are not JSON Schema Draft 7 formats, so AJV warns. Stripping them before validation is safe because:

1. The `format` keyword is only a semantic validation hint
2. The MCP server validates its own inputs
3. AJV already ignores these formats ("ignored in schema") — we just prevent the warning

This fixes warnings from all 9 affected Google Cloud MCP servers plus any future MCP server using custom format specifiers.

@Cdddo @fwang , I fixed the issue with PR #32966.

Root cause: MiMo/GLM-5.2/Xiaomi require tool role messages to have `content` as a plain string, not `ContentPart[]` array. The AI SDK sends tool results as `[{type: "tool-result", output: {type: "text", value: "..." }}]`, which these providers reject with 400 errors.

Fix: Added provider-specific transform that flattens single-part tool results to plain strings for affected providers. Multi-part content is preserved as array (providers that don't support it will error, which signals the limitation clearly.

@Spirit597 @MrMushrooooom , I fixed the issue with PR #32966.

Root cause: GLM-5.2 (and Xiaomi/MiMo) require tool role `messages[].content` to be a plain string, not `ContentPart[]` array. This is the same root cause as #32613.

Fix: Added a provider transform that flattens single-part tool results to strings for providers in the `FLATTEN_TOOL_CONTENT_PROVIDERS` list (mimo, glm, xiaomi). Extension point: add more provider IDs to the tuple to handle similar cases.
